Z||000013||Fformula88||12-01-2001||10:15 AM||||The 84's getted dumped on because of their reputation from fires, because they didn't live up to expectations because of not offering enough horsepower, and now because they are the oldest, and generally not in really good condition.<P>I have no problems with the 84's, and a nice condition 84 is as good as any other Fiero IMO.  They don't have any 6 cyl's, but neither do the majority of 85-88's eiher.<P>This is our 85 SE.  Looks just like the 84's and I wouldn't consider it ugly at all.  It actually gets more looks and compliments than my bright red Formula!!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/whitefiero1.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/whitefiero2.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulasig.JPG">             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">     <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6<p>[This message has been edited by Fformula88 (edited 12-01-2001).]||||reg||1
